From dd7b617b7596d61e37ab5645d1660919514b4c28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuxi Luo <yl5960@columbia.edu>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:28:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(equity): move FMP calls to the /stable/ API

FMP no longer serves the legacy /api/v3 and /api/v4 endpoints to keys
created after 2025-08-31 (every call returns 403 "Legacy Endpoint"), so
generate_financial_analysis.py could not fetch any data with a new key.

- Route all FMP requests through _fmp_get(), which calls /stable/ and
  re-raises errors without the request URL. requests puts the full URL,
  apikey included, into its exception messages, which were printed to
  the console and written into news_summary.md.
- Copy renamed stable fields back to their v3 names (calendarYear,
  priceEarningsRatio, debtEquityRatio, enterpriseValueOverEBITDA, mktCap,
  ...) so financial_data_processor, create_equity_report and the PDF
  generator keep working unchanged. ROE/ROA and P/E, P/B moved between
  the ratios and key-metrics endpoints and are copied back as well.
- Target price now uses /price-target-consensus: the per-analyst feed the
  v4 call read is premium-only on the stable API.
- Shares outstanding come from /shares-float (no longer in /quote).
- Map the CLI's --period quarterly to the "quarter" value FMP expects.
- News uses /stable/news/stock; on the free plan it returns 402 and the
  pipeline continues without news, as it already did when news was empty.
